   458	- **The road Oxhollow–Lowmarch (flag):** south down a broad valley of alder and rough pasture, small fords, halting-grounds; on the fourth day two hundred yards of moss crossed by a causeway of laid logs (the carter's father's), about one log in six rotten at the heart. It reaches Lowmarch's river on the west bank and crosses by the ferry.
