   534	## AFTER MOVEMENT 5 — chapters 31–37, dusk of day 96 to day 100 past the Line (drafted 2026-10-11, author claude-opus-5-5, NO-SOURCE method)
   535	
   536	### Coordinator rulings (binding)
   537	- **Deployment since the Line: THIRTEEN.** One at the ford (day 53) and twelve in the Ring on the night of the 96th, each priced and billed in the night log: Iron read; Shadow (once, ten strides); Wind; Pressure; Ember (one point on the knife's tip); Blade (an edge on Lira's knife); Anchor (perception only — a deliberate release counts); Storm lanes one, two and three (ten / ten / twelve counts; the body read lost while the air is held); Wind a second time; Compression at contact, late. The two noon tests of the 96th are left out of the number, unexplained. All capability rules held.
   538	- **Shadow has been used ONCE and remains sealed.** Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln had the sightline; Oryn was screened and saw him arrive, not come; the pack is no witness. Oryn cannot identify Seln as its source. Seln struck Cael's second reason for silence ("I shall not be a reason… I should sooner have her told what may be done to her than be used to keep her ignorant") WITHOUT offering to be known as the source: Movement 6 tells her sources by Path, not by person, and the seal serves again at the Stair.
   539	- **The Ring:** nine hounds counted on the white; two dead by Brom's bolts (thirteen feet; six feet); seven away "north and south along the line's outside", direction unobserved. The crossbow was on the mule; Seln fetched it during the retreat round the floor and Brom spanned it by hand. Bolts: six, five in the sleeve from the 97th. Geometry as closed in Movement 4.
   540	- **Inside the line** no companion Path was used: Oryn's hands had nothing ("Nothing in my hands"); cloth and knees. Nobody has theorized why the fragments answered. *Quieting* has still not been said. "Compact" has been said aloud once, by Seln. Nothing is known of where the file is, what it says or why; dating stops at "five years… maybe six". Seln's map memory (maps with holes) is open; he asked for the carter's map.
   541	- **The tenth fragment — Tide-adjacent — was acquired on the 100th** in Oryn's long reading (minute twenty-one); the notice is exact; "More than one" is said. **Cael let it happen without telling her first, with the covenant written beforehand, and told her the minute it was over. The page treats it as a wrong he did knowingly**: all four companions named it for what it is, he agreed that refusing would be right, and he chose against it. Writing it first made it knowing, not permitted. Oryn does NOT yet know the mechanism: her own naming of what was done, her terms and its cost to him are Movement 6's first scene. Integration cost is not yet paid.
   542	- **Bodies:** Lira — right ankle gone a third time; forearm bitten and held, mended by Oryn outside the line (one mending "the size of two"), arm in a sling, walking flat-footed on Oryn's order; tibia mended earlier. Karis — throat, mended. Brom — ONE hand, the pads of FOUR fingers cut by the string, mended, four dark lines; no string until the 100th. Cael — the calf opened again on a stone (bound, closing by itself, not mended); left forearm (Compression's bill); ribs whole on the 99th. Oryn spent "three in two days… that's a route".
   543	- **Money:** 108 in hand, unchanged. **Names:** none minted. **Length:** about 35,800 at draft; the Ring's 10,858 words accepted as earned.
