   571	*Updated after repair r1 (see `REPAIR-REPORT-r1.md`). Facts changed: Brom's hurt is ONE hand, four finger-pads; Oryn's rule for it is "Nothing on the string for three days"; Seln strikes Cael's second reason without offering to be known to Oryn; Lira's arm was first bound with Brom's folded cuff and strips of Oryn's shirt, her linen being on the mule; Cael's calf stays in Karis's blanket strip from the 96th until the yard on the 99th and is never bound by Oryn; the hound that Cael throws is let go by and helped on its way, after the jaws are levered open with the hilt of Lira's knife; the second lock is struck from behind, and he goes down onto the left forearm. Word counts, metrics and line numbers elsewhere in this report are the pre-repair figures; the markers it lists are filled.*
   572	
   573	**Calendar.** The morning of the **hundredth day past the Line**, in Thornwater's back room, in the twenty-first minute of the long reading. No season, month or English weekday name is on the page ("first snow", "the snow", "the harvest", "frost"). Days on the page: 96 (sunset to night), 97, 98, 99, 100. Weather: frost every night; a north wind on the Fallow; ice on Thornwater's trough.
   574	
   575	**Where everyone is.** Cael on the plank table with Oryn's hands on him, the door shut. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln in or about the loft over the barn, with all three boxes and the covenant leaf in Hesk's book. The mule in Thornwater's yard. Five of the hold's people waiting until after noon.
   576	
   577	**Cael.** Eighteen. **Ten confirmed fragments** from the twentieth minute: the tenth is Tide-adjacent, partial, Iron, self and contact, *Acquisition: directed. Engagement: clinical — non-hostile.* It has not been tried, and its cost has not begun. The uncounted anomaly is untouched and unmentioned in this movement. **Deployment since the Line: thirteen** (the ford; twelve in the Ring on the 96th), as his log has it; the noon tests of the 96th are noted in the log as left out. Shadow used **once**. Ribs whole, the tape off on the 99th. Calf closed; it stayed in Karis's blanket strip from the night of the 96th until Oryn undid the knot in the yard on the 99th. Left forearm bruised and working (he came down on it under the hound's weight in the second lock). He knows that refusing would have been right and that the leaf permitted nothing; he chose against it and means to answer for it. He has told Oryn two things: that what she saw on the hill was his doing, and, in the last minute, "I need to tell you what I am." He has told nobody why anything answered him inside, and has not told Lira since when he knew. Three letters still unanswered.
   578	
   579	**Lira.** Wind; Iron, Rank One. No burst. **Left forearm bitten through on the 96th, mended at the line; slung, and under the order until first snow** (nothing held, struck or caught). **Right ankle over a third time, taped, not mended**; she walks on the whole sole. The new tibia was run on for twenty yards and held. She knows that he chose not to act on the floor and that he had known he could; she has said "Later." and is keeping it. Her long knife is blunt.
   580	
   581	**Brom.** Iron Skin; Copper. **One hand, four finger-pads** laid open on the string, mended at noon on the 97th (four dark lines); **nothing on the string for three days, until the hundredth**. The folded linen cuff that he kept inside his shirt went to pad Lira's arm at the rim. He shot twice and killed twice. He carried the middle box through the whole of the Ring. He has the bill; the bow is his to carry and Karis has had the sleeve.
   582	
   583	**Karis.** Ember; Iron, Rank Three. **Nine points and eight joins for a count of six at the line on the 96th**; about a tenth left that night; nothing since. Throat mended on the 97th; hoarse single words by the 99th. Holds: eleven Ring sheets, dry, not yet looked at; the box unopened; the carter's map with three rings (two still *guess*) and Seln's charcoal sheet; her leaf *Where / Entered as said / Blank. Stamped. Filed.*; the stub and the entry against herself of the 99th. The two torn leaves lay on the loft's boards. She has asked him nothing.
   584	
   585	**Seln.** Shadow; Bronze. Unmarked. He fetched the bow, opened the jaws, carried Karis to the stone and called "Back". He has said "Compact" aloud once. He has given what he remembers of eight sheets and has refused to guess the file; nobody knows what such a file holds. He has struck Cael's second reason himself ("I should sooner have her told what may be done to her than be used to keep her ignorant") **without offering to be known to Oryn as a source**; the seal stands. **The case is on its strap, on him, shut.**
   586	
   587	**Oryn.** Tide; Iron, Rank Four. Three mendings on the crew in two days; none since. She has crossed the line eight times alone at dawn on the 98th, which only Cael saw. She has read him five times at the surface and once at depth, and has found movement, "more than one", and no banks. She felt something change in him in the twentieth minute; she has been told that he did it and that he must tell her what he is; **she does not know the mechanism**. Thornwater's bench is owed four days and is put off until after noon.
   588	
   589	**Objects and money.** Board purse unchanged: **a hundred and thirty-two earned; a hundred and eight in hand.** The Fallow hundred lies in Pike's box; no instruments were found; the posting (five strokes) is in Hesk's book. The crossbow, with **five bolts**, is with the crew; its spanning hook is in the mule's near-side pannier. One bolt lies on the Ring's floor. Six blankets returned, one a hand narrow. The rope is still owed.
   590	
   591	**Hounds.** Nine came; two are dead (one on the floor, one drawn off a hundred yards south of the stone, outside the line); **seven went north and south along the line's outside** on the night of the 96th and were not seen, tracked or heard again.
   592	
   593	**Pike's book and the wall.** Unchanged: seven lines; tenth; Teague nine up. The Fallow line has not been said. The two HOLD slips are unresolved on the page.
   594	
   595	**Who knows what.** The mechanism: the five. Oryn knows that he can do, inside a line, what no Path can; she saw Wind, a light, and heard an edge ring; she did not see the Shadow use and cannot attribute his arrival at Karis. Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln saw it. All six know that the registry's iron stands on the line, that maps were drawn with a blank there, and that the posting was a question which their coming out has answered. Nobody knows where the file is, what it says, or why. Nobody has said why the fragments answer inside.
   596	
   597	**Open threads.** The telling, on the table, owed that minute. What it cost her, if anything. A leaf in a loft to be fetched and read. *Later*, on Lira's side. Seven hounds. A report going west with six on it. An arm slung until the snow, and an ankle that nobody has mended. Eleven sheets not yet looked at. Two rings marked *guess*. The top gate of a round, eleven days north.
