   138	1. **Karis's rank.** The packet lists the five sigils as "Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4". The edition's Karis is Iron, Rank Three, retained (BOOK_MAP §1; every ledger block). I wrote "An Ember: Iron, third rank" (42:7) and "five Paths, and three tiers".
   139	2. **"The still place" is already in the edition's Books 5 and 6.** Cael's logs there call the anomaly "the still place from session nine" (Book 5 ch1, ch45, ch60) and "the still place I don't count" (Book 6 ch34). Book 7's map says the phrase arrives in Movement 8. I followed the packet: this movement never uses it ("something there that did not flow"; "a place in the middle of himself"). The series needs one answer.
   140	3. **"Tomorrow makes three."** The second pole is protected and is printed as the map gives it. On this edition's days it is written at the well as the 111th breaks; one site has been entered. I have not glossed it and cannot make the three add up; the coordinator may know what the line counts.
   141	4. **Practice and the deployment number.** Eleven leans of Wind in the yard on the 101st are entered in the log as practice and kept out of "Deployment since the Line: thirteen" (39:245–247), with his reason. If the number should move, it is one log line.
   142	5. **Her answer is withheld from the reader as well as from him.** In her window she "knew what she would have said" and does not say it over. My first draft stated it; I took it out so that nothing on the page supplies consent after the fact.
   143	6. **Oryn's five further days** are spent on Lira's arm (the eighth mark slow on the 106th). That is my staging, to make the packet's figures (nine and eleven on the 104th; seventeen at Oxhollow on the 110th) come out of one honest sum. It costs her route five days and puts them, against her instruction, on Lira.
   144	7. **"North", and Millrace.** The ledger puts Millrace a day south of Lowmarch, and Lowmarch two days west of Thornwater; the packet sends Oryn north out of the gate and has her at Millrace's table on the 113th. I sent her north by the wicket and bent the road west and south along a water; the gate is not named and no distance is given.
   145	8. **Seln's Path** is said aloud once in the barn (42:11, "A Shadow, Bronze") with Oryn at her bench across the yard. It is never said in her hearing. Her hand on his shoulder in the loft (44, second scene) is left unread by Cael.
   146	9. **Lira guesses "a thirty-two"** (43, first scene). It is a guess about a numeral, answered by Karis's fourth sentence; it is there to make Movement 7's stakes land.
   147	10. **Apple words near the birthday.** "One was picked a month before the other"; "came down a fortnight after it"; "meal before the snow's a week old". They count apples, and carry no season name and no count to or from a birthday; I flag them in case #42/#48 is read more strictly.
   148	11. **"The last time"** is how Lira and Seln refer to the birthday before this one (40:185, 40:311). No interval is given. The chapter is titled "Six Places" so that the number is first heard from Lira.
   149	12. **The founding stone** is a new piece of Ostrand: an old gate from which the city counts its years. No year is given.
