   122	
   123	It was also how the five paid for their bread there. Nobody had struck a bargain. The steading's woman had looked at Brom's shoulders on the first evening, and at the height of her loft, and had said that her own men were two short; and Brom had said that he would be glad of something to lift.
   124	
