     4	
     5	She had waited seven days to do it. Cael had watched her carry that restraint across the Fallow and up a ladder and through a birthday, with eleven sheets lying dry in the dark not six feet from her blanket; and he had understood that it was a kind of manners. She would not look at a thing until she could look at all of it.
