editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-38.md:187:"A ruled matter is not a pending matter," said Karis. "The code's very particular about it, in a section about enrollees under orders that haven't yet taken effect. Once the seat has ruled, the proceeding is concluded. If the ruling revokes an enrollment, the revocation takes effect on a date, and until that date the enrollee is still an enrollee in standing, under an order. And an enrollee in standing may withdraw." She put her finger on a line in the brown ink. "And the house enters it in these words."
