editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-249-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-250-He did not write the cache in the book.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-251-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-252-He sat at the sill with the satchel on it and the book open and Hesk's pen in his hand, and the court below him dark, and the fountain going up black and coming down white, and he did not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-253-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md:254:He had written everything for years. Every notice word for word, every price. The book was where a thing went to be true. And Seln had sat across the table and asked where it was written, and when he had answered, Seln had said *Under the bed*. In a voice that cost nothing, he had said, *A thing told three times is a thing on its way to being known.* The case had been kept twelve years by a man who had never once described it to anybody. Cael did not think he would last twelve hours if he started writing it down.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-255-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-256-So he wrote what he could.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-257-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-258-*Day 88. Five in Karis's room by three stairs across an hour. The case opened. What was in it does not go into a book. It is in a room with two keys, and the five of us have it, and that is where it will stay.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-37.md-259-
