editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-107-The fountain went on in the middle of it, as it did all year, with a crust of ice round the rim of the basin and the water going up black and coming down white in the light from the residence windows. He went round it at a walk, past the dark bulk of the lecture range and the records hall with its one lamp burning in the side window, which was Bracken's lamp and burned there every night of the year whether Bracken was under it or not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-108-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-109-At the top of the library, four floors up, the reading room's window was lit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-110-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md:111:It was lit the way it was lit every night of the year, a yellow square at the top of the dark building, with the lamp set close to the glass so that you could see it from the north wall and the gate lodge and, Seln had once said, from the ferry landing at the foot of the bluff. The whole valley knew that window. A coat at the foot of the road could have told you the hour by it: lit at dusk, out somewhere between the tenth bell and the eleventh, never once dark before the ninth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-112-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-113-Tonight it was lit exactly the same.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-114-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-115-He went in at the library's front door. *Door*, he told it, as his hand went to the iron ring. *Heavy. It keeps the cold out.* The lower hall was warm and smelled of lamp oil and old paper and the stove at the far end. Under the green-shaded lamps at the long tables two readers sat with their heads down. One was a fourth-year from the Ash faculty with a code open and his chin on his fist, and the other a girl Cael did not know, asleep with her cheek on her own notes. The night porter sat in his box by the stair with a newspaper. He looked up, saw a student going up to the reading rooms, and looked down.
