editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-193-She took the first one from the top of the first row. She drew the shaded lamp an inch nearer and held the two sheets under it, and Cael saw that they were both in the same hand, small and round and perfectly level, the copying hand of the wing that had filled the floor schedule on the refectory door every week for two years.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-194-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md:195:"The first sheet is a copy of a station's Kindling record," said Karis. She read it in her plain voice, the one she used for a citation, giving each word its weight and no more. "*River station, the fourth district. Entry of the twelfth. A girl of the town. Reading at the frame: Current, second rank. Keeper's note at the margin: reads into Mire. Strong.*" She laid it face up in front of her. "That's the keeper's hand copied. You can see where he pressed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-35.md-196-
