editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-36.md-28-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-36.md-29-He had spent all year writing himself down. Every Fifth-day in wing three he had stood in front of three cards and fought at a rate the house had chosen for him, a smaller man than the one he was, entered in the house's book at a figure that breathed and never rose. He had paid for it every week and called it a cost. But he had chosen it. He had sat at a long table with the people who mattered to him and decided, in ink, how much of himself to show, and he could have stopped any Fifth-day he liked. None of the twenty-three had chosen anything. Somebody had looked at what they were and stamped the page to say they were something less, and they had never even been told there was a page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-36.md-30-
