    38	
    39	- **Shadow is used once in this movement**, unseen and never attributable. That is its second and last use in the book.
    40	- **The rim saw a practitioner walk out declaring, and saw nothing work inside.** Teague saw the same and asks nothing.
    41	- Faceless: no seals, no names, no office. The specialist is not the Ostrand-road woman: the same craft, a different weight in the laying.
    42	- The case is untouched. The index and the stroke-and-bar are not decoded. Nobody theorizes.
    43	- Oryn joins as a stop on her route, never as "sixth," never "join." The Stair slip's three hundred is taken and never paid.
    44	- Teague's crew is unnamed, including in Teague's window. The healer of no Path does not appear until M8.
    45	
    46	## What the author owns
    47	
    48	The Lowmarch room; Millrace's texture; Oryn's patients; the road lesson's sensation; the chamber's cold; the stalemate's small human business; the ascent's suspense inside the planted rules; the rim action's choreography; the six hours; both windows.
    49	
    50	## Where we leave pressure
    51	
    52	Day 115, at the stone in full sun. The kit is on Brom's good shoulder and his bad one is mended once. Lira's arm is closed again with the sling higher. The ledger is in Seln's coat; twenty-nine sheets and forty-one kinds. A brass edge lies on a map. A dead man's last word was *bearing*. "We're going to go look."

