editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:43:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** arrives by carter: “Six went in. Six came out.” It lands against Cael's memory of Gault's last line, *The instruments will not see its like.* Gault's physical leaf remains in the west with the withdrawal file and is not among the party's papers. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D5, N5] Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:104:**Who knows the cache/falsification history:** the five travelers plus Vastin. Vastin does not know the integration mechanism. Ephram, Withrow, Bracken, Ilsev, Havel, Rooke, Gault, Jent and the public know neither. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit N6]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:123:- **Karis's three numbered boxes** (left, middle, right; middle with one corner worn white): the field archive, masonry chips, registry printed continental sheet and Ternhall brass straightedge. The printed sheet is marked *ridge* and *Shelf; a pine; water at 36*. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D3, N4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:23:- **Objects:** a two-wheeled cart; a brown gelding with one white foot; three numbered boxes and Seln's locked case under one canvas; the pooled Book 6 purse; two no-return-address letters, to Hesk and Vell, written at the shelf and held for the first westbound carrier. Daeva's reply already went west from the first water beyond the Line. The registry's printed continental sheet and the Ternhall straightedge are in Karis's middle box. Karis has marked the sheet *ridge* and *Shelf; a pine; water at 36*. Lira's separate route book reads *Ridge: one horse, three boxes by hand. Scree: by hand again. Shelf.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D3, D5, N3, N4, N7; coordinator O2 (the case rides under the canvas)]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:24:- **Compact posture:** the file reads *Status: active non-compliance, observation priority escalated.* Asset-restriction is *pending jurisdiction*: it will be served within the hour if any one of the four enrolled names is written in a book inside a district. The last watcher turned back at the provincial marker. The author of the fifth file line is unnamed, and no office is named on it. Vastin remains inside as Archmarshal / the certifying office and returned the closing summary without annotation. Gault remains evaluator of record. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit C3, D5]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:35:- **Karis:** holds the field archive: **52 sheets** of copied walls (Ring 11 / Stair 29 / Hall 12); the kit's **field ledger** (given her by Seln on the road home); the carter's map with **four circles and the bearing**; the Ternhall straightedge. She named the Quieting. Her hypothesis stays unentered. She has the inn's back room for the sheets.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:42:- **Objects:** the kit (case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar mark and a bright point, mallet); the ledger; the 52 sheets; the map; **two brass straightedges** (Ternhall's; Hesk's, arrived on the last ferry). Both touch the three paced centres without daylight, **in Cael's hand as in anyone's** (Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair of error). Also three boxes, Seln's case, one mule (the crew's), and Oryn's crossbow with one bolt left in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Lira** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M2: 1,800 (day 53, the bar at dusk without Wind: fast, with nothing at the end) · M3: 1,800 (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose; "That was me. The loud thing.") · M5: 2,000 (days 97–98: one arm, the order, "Later" kept; walking flat-footed because Oryn said) · M6: 2,000 (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow somebody else spans) | Everything she knows (the log, the fragments); her Fenmark and Norhold history; her want; her body's counts | Why Cael's fragments work inside before he tells her (day 110); any escalation of Cael–Lira past what the source shows (warmth and covenant, not declaration); asking for the ankle twice |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-41.md:147:It had not been the sourness that she minded. It had been a small bald man saying, without the least unkindness, that she would not tell a keeper from an eater in the one basket on the one day. He had not been talking about method. He had been talking about fruit. But it was the best sentence on method that anybody had said to her since Ternhall, and she had gone up the ladder afterward and lain awake over it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-40.md:163:It was Brom who began the song. He had a great deal of voice and no notion where to put it, and he got through the first line by himself. Lira came in on the second with the words that they used at Fenmark, which were not Brom's words, and the two of them stopped and looked at each other across a bowl.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-40.md:171:"There is a third verse, at Ternhall, in the old tongue." Karis had put down her spoon. "Nobody knows what it means. I can't sing, so I shall say it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-40.md:237:Gault had signed a figure for him every week for two years, to the decimal. He had ended by writing that no instrument would have such a thing to measure again. And here was a man with one arm and a horn ink-pot, who had never owned an instrument in his life, and who had written down in six words what six people did. There had been nothing at that place to recover. He had put that down too.

