editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-42.md:3:Karis read out her second finding on the hundred and sixth morning, and she began it with a table that all of them had seen made.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-42.md:113:"I'll read it at the fortnight," she said, over her shoulder. "That's the hundred and tenth. If it's taken by then, it's taken."
