editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-38-The deliberate quieter movement. Its reason: integration cost, the midpoint disclosure and the birthday, between the Ring and the Stair. Its action is learning. Cael turns nineteen with the lights on inside himself; the Quieting gets its name; Lira hears it first; and the instrument gets a rule before it is ever turned outward. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-39-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:40:- **The telling on the table** is explicitly a retelling to Oryn of what Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln already established in edition B6: his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the station plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word replaced the old name; the Arbiter then went dark. Sources are named by Path, not by person, except the three Oryn has touched. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] The notice said aloud. The page fetched from the loft and read twice in its counted places. **Her answer** (protected): "So I couldn't read you because…" … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone… I want to be the one you tell." Oryn's new condition governs Tide reading outward: self first, then ask first every time. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4] "You're the colour of the wall…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:41:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-42-- **Karis documents** in a dry-hinge voice ("For now."; "You have an instrument now. It's not mine… I'm entering that I know that.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-43-- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** arrives by carter: “Six went in. Six came out.” It lands against Cael's memory of Gault's last line, *The instruments will not see its like.* Gault's physical leaf remains in the west with the withdrawal file and is not among the party's papers. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D5, N5] Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:44:- **The first self-reading** that night, alone, as she set it. Ten flows and no banks (a limit of the reading, written above everything else). Then **the place session nine logged**: not a current, not the tenth, not any of the nine; near the middle, where everything is nearer; the ten go *round* it. Three things he can count. It is **not named**: no "still place" yet. The inventory, and **the three words retired with the reason** (protected). "Hundred and two in hand; six to the hold for the room and the kid."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets one numbered rubbing to each upright, each upright's height recorded [corrected at M4 close]); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, no ranking, Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-46-- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-47-- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:48:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-49-- **Oryn's window north (111–112):** the spare rope, the road bending, what she carries in her head. It ends before Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-50-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-51-## What must remain true / withheld
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-52-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:53:- **The still place is not named here.** It is "a place that does not flow." The phrase arrives in M8.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-54-- **Karis's hypothesis is never stated**, in dialogue or in her window. **[UNBOUND] appears once**, aloud, as a limit.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-55-- The debt to Oryn (telling her the self-reading) is **owed**, with the day set by her. It is not paid in M6.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-56-- No reading of anyone but himself. The tenth is used on no one else.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-64-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-65-## Where we leave pressure
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md-66-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:67:Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-16-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-17-- **Where/when:** the switchback shelf above an unnamed valley, the second camp beyond the Registry Line and the first fire beyond it. Book 7 dates everything *past the Line*: Book 6's Sixth-day from Ostrand is Book 7's **second day past the Line** (edition B6 ch58–60; B6 CLOSED M9 ledger). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A1, D4, N1]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-18-- **Party: FIVE.** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln. Ephram stayed at Halcenvane with his right shoulder set and a month in a sling. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D3]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:19:- **Cael:** eighteen. **Nine confirmed fragments + the Tide-adjacent anomaly**, uncounted, under the standing words *Still open. Still real. Patience.* No injury open: the Crown-yard left-forearm bruise is a week from gone, and the ten-count road bill has cleared. Hesk's satchel holds the current log (about a third of its leaves left); the full old volume, with Hesk's letters under its front board; the observation notebook; and the two held no-return-address letters to Hesk and Vell. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D1, D3, N2, N3; coordinator O1 (the Velmere letter is not carried)]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-20-- **The seal:** Shadow-adjacent is sealed from any witness who could carry the seeing west, because a defector's tradecraft in Cael's hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition. It costs from waking and drifts at dusk. Cael leaves it sealed past the Line; deployment since the Line is none. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D1, D3; F-rerun F2.4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-21-- **Companions:** Lira, Wind, Iron R1 retained; Silver evaluation declined at full price. Brom, Iron Skin, Copper formal for good, continental Copper champion; Iron finding unsigned. He left the last Velmere letter sealed and unopened on his table at Halcenvane, with the unsigned finding; he carries no family letter east (edition B6 ch56). Karis, Ember, Iron R3 retained; research standing, budget/allocation, annex, archive privileges and restricted-collection access lapsed; three boxes made into a field archive. Seln, Shadow, Bronze, fifteen years' service; left without notice or form, four keys surrendered; brought the locked case east in his own satchel; it now rides under the canvas. All five have no open injury. Lira and Brom have read the log. Karis sees demonstrations, not the log. Seln has known the mechanism since edition B6 ch37; he recognized that Cael kept his file; his “twice more” allowance remains two. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D2, B5, C2; coordinator O1, O2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-22-- **Who knows:** the integration mechanism is known to the five travelers and nobody else. The cache/falsification history is known to those five plus Vastin; Vastin does not know the mechanism. Ephram knows only the departure and the deliberately managed band. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit N6]
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-28-### Ending (Book 7 close, days 129–131 — must match the source and Book 8 Ch1)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-29-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-30-- **Where/when:** Lowmarch in first snow on the 129th day past the Line. The ferry's last run on the 130th. Oryn's letter by carter on the morning of the 131st. Book 8 Ch1 opens on the 131st.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:31:- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-32-- **The rule on the tenth, in Oryn's hand and his:** *ask first, every time.* It was paid once, by not reading Teague.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-33-- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-34-- **Brom:** right shoulder bolted on the Stair and mended, reopened in the Hall and mended a second time ("Twice… not three times this season"). Then bound by Teague's healer of no Path and carried guarded. Carries the kit and the middle box.
--
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-39-- **Pike's board:** **nine completed lines** under the five names (the last three are the traverse, the Ring and the Stair). The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The **season line** has been read aloud. **No line number entered**: "First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." The five names stay **eleventh** on the wall, unchanged.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-40-- **Teague:** "After the thaw. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) stays at Lowmarch through the cold term. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the cold term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch24 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-41-- **Money:** **ninety-six in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn for the back room). Three hundred entered as taken and never to be paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:42:- **Objects:** the kit (case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar mark and a bright point, mallet); the ledger; the 52 sheets; the map; **two brass straightedges** (Ternhall's; Hesk's, arrived on the last ferry). Both touch the three paced centres without daylight, **in Cael's hand as in anyone's** (Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair of error). Also three boxes, Seln's case, one mule (the crew's), and Oryn's crossbow with one bolt left in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:43:- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **about four hundred and forty yards' radius** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-44-- **The Compact:** knows quiet ground exists and what it does, and which crew walks out of it (a completion report on the Fallow contract; the rim on the Stair saw a practitioner walk out *declaring*). **It does not know that anything works inside.** Asset-restriction is still pending. The nameless second Anchor hand: "the account's getting longer."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-45-- **Letters west on the last ferry:** to Hesk ("Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof…") and to Vell ("There's a second ledger on the continent…").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md-46-- **Last paragraph:** verbatim (§10, Ch24).
--
