editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-36.md-130-
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-36.md:131:"The registry corrects them. At Kindling, when the station reads them. Downward, by a form, for as long as it has had paper to write the form on. That is what I have carried."
