   147	10. **Apple words near the birthday.** "One was picked a month before the other"; "came down a fortnight after it"; "meal before the snow's a week old". They count apples, and carry no season name and no count to or from a birthday; I flag them in case #42/#48 is read more strictly.
   148	11. **"The last time"** is how Lira and Seln refer to the birthday before this one (40:185, 40:311). No interval is given. The chapter is titled "Six Places" so that the number is first heard from Lira.
   149	12. **The founding stone** is a new piece of Ostrand: an old gate from which the city counts its years. No year is given.
