+   old: `"I was wrong about apples." Karis rested her throat, and went on. "I looked into one basket, on one day, and I said *two*. A man who had kept those trees for twenty-six years showed me three. This is one basket." Her hand went round the eleven strips. "I have one floor. If a hook is cut a little wide on the ninth stone, I cannot tell whether that is a different kind, or the same kind and a tired arm. Nobody could, from here. So I shall count. And I shall not number the kinds from one site."`
