+9. `manuscript/chapter-41.md`
+   old: `Eleven stones, on one floor, rubbed in one afternoon by one hand. Every difference on those strips was a difference that she could not weigh. A wide hook might be a word. It might be a mason whose arm was tired at the ninth stone, or a flaw in the grey, or her own pencil slipping while Lira shifted her palm. She could not ask the mason. She could not go back to the stone.`
